06)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Fluoroquinolones are contraindicated or require caution in patients with specific comorbidities\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Certain conditions increase the risk of adverse outcomes when fluoroquinolones are administered. For instance, lomefloxacin is cautioned in patients with hepatic impairment, requiring liver function monitoring [Data: Relationships (3581)]. Separately, while not directly involving a fluoroquinolone, ibuprofen is contraindicated in acute cerebrovascular disease—a relevant consideration given that NSAIDs are commonly co-prescribed with antibiotics for pain or inflammation, and oxygenfloxacin specifically interacts with NSAIDs [Data: Relationships (6303, 40847)]. Although tacrolimus (not a fluoroquinolone) is contraindicated in acute kidney injury, the association of fluoroquinolones like oxygenfloxacin with nephrotoxicity (e.g., when combined with polymyxin E) further supports cautious use in renal impairment [Data: Relationships (5485, 12890)]. These contraindications and cautions reflect the need for comprehensive patient assessment prior to fluoroquinolone prescription.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Ciprofloxacin is linked to tendon disorders, a known class risk for fluoroquinolones\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Ciprofloxacin is explicitly associated with tendon disorders (肌腱病症), a well-documented adverse effect within the fluoroquinolone class that can include tendinitis and tendon rupture, particularly in older adults or those on corticosteroids [Data: Relationships (13917)]. Although the provided evidence cites this reaction under a broader discussion of fluoroquinolone toxicities, the direct relationship between ciprofloxacin and tendon pathology is clearly stated in the source material [Data: Entities (7289); Relationships (13917)]. This finding aligns with regulatory warnings issued globally and reinforces the necessity of informing patients about early symptoms of tendon damage during treatment.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Drug formulation and co-administration with antacids significantly alter fluoroquinolone absorption\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The bioavailability of fluoroquinolones is highly susceptible to interference from cation-containing compounds. Specifically, aluminum- and magnesium-based antacids reduce the oral absorption of levofloxacin (a close analog of oxygenfloxacin), and similar chelation effects are noted for oxygenfloxacin with magnesium, aluminum, iron, and zinc preparations [Data: Relationships (37247, 40847)]. This physicochemical interaction forms insoluble complexes in the gastrointestinal tract, drastically lowering systemic drug exposure and potentially compromising therapeutic efficacy. Clinicians are advised to separate dosing times or avoid concurrent use altogether, reflecting a critical administration consideration for this antibiotic class [Data: Entities (4368, 6173); Relationships (37247, 40847)].\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community poses a high clinical impact due to the serious and potentially life-threatening adverse effects and drug interactions associated with widely used fluoroquinolone antibiotics.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782128544, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1554, "prompt_tokens": 7086, "total_tokens": 8640, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 0}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"Fluoroquinolone Antibiotics and Associated Adverse Effects\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community 